# Route each subject area's definitions to the office accountable for it, so
# the right reviewers are required automatically and the merged pull request
# becomes the approval record.
#
# TODO: replace the placeholder team handles below with real GitHub teams.
# Until a team exists, a review requirement pointing at it is silently
# ineffective -- GitHub does not warn about an unknown owner. Verify with
# Settings -> Branches -> require review from Code Owners, then open a test PR.
#
# The office named here must match the owner in the term files themselves.
# Nothing enforces that automatically; it is checked at review time.

# The site configuration, the glossary, and the domain affect every subject area.
/dgo-atlas.yaml                                          @unmc-vcr/data-governance-program
/governance/glossary.yaml                               @unmc-vcr/data-governance-program
/governance/research_administration/research_administration.yaml  @unmc-vcr/data-governance-program

# The organization registry decides who can hold a role at all.
/governance/organization.yaml                           @unmc-vcr/data-governance-program

# Subject areas, one line per directory. The directory pattern covers the
# subject-area file and every term file under terms/, so a new term is routed
# to the right office without touching this file.
/governance/research_administration/clinical_research/  @unmc-vcr/clinical-research-office
/governance/research_administration/sponsored_programs/ @unmc-vcr/sponsored-programs-office

# Published narrative and standards.
/content/                                               @unmc-vcr/data-governance-program

# The build itself.
/pyproject.toml                                         @unmc-vcr/data-governance-program
/uv.lock                                                @unmc-vcr/data-governance-program
/.github/                                               @unmc-vcr/data-governance-program
